File Index

/RolesPage.tsx
Purpose: Phase G Roles tab — "your access" card always visible (master/key/account, with local tier + hub global role for account actors); a management table that only renders when GET /api/roles succeeds (a 403 there just means "you can't manage roles," not an error — hidden, not shown-and-broken). Grant form's tier select is capped at the same ceiling the server enforces (never offers 'owner') so a forced-past-the-UI request is the only way to even try, and the server still 400s that too. Same "hide what you can't do, server enforces it for real" convention as auth-client's AdminPage. 2026-08-16, two live bugs same day: (1) a user typed their USERNAME into the grant form's "Account ID" field (nothing showed them the real value), silently granting a role to a string matching no real session — first fixed by showing the real accountId with a "use it" self-fill button; (2) superseded hours later by removing the "Account ID" field entirely — the grant form now takes ONLY a username (`api.setRole(username, tier)`, POSTs to `/api/roles`), and the server resolves it to the real accountId itself. The "your access" card's self-fill button now fills `me.username` instead.

/RolesPage.test.tsx
Purpose: Roles tab tests: plain-user standing with no table, master standing text, grant list rendering + tier options excluding 'owner', granting a role by username and seeing the list refresh, own-username display + the "use it" fill-in button, an unknown-username 404 surfacing as a toast (all 2026-08-16).
